# Anchor zero-copy

Hot accounts (`VaultState`, nullifiers, large configs) use zero-copy — not `Account<'info, T>` heap deserialize.

## Required pattern

```rust
#[account(zero_copy)]
#[repr(C)]
pub struct VaultState {
    pub authority: Pubkey,
    // ... fixed fields ...
    pub bump: u8,
    pub _padding: [u8; 7], // explicit; keep 8-byte alignment
}
```

- Always `#[repr(C)]` + explicit padding; never rely on Rust field reordering
- Prefer `AccountLoader<'info, T>` in contexts; use `.load()` / `.load_mut()`
- Assert size/alignment in tests or `const` checks when adding fields
- Checked math on reserves (`checked_add` / `checked_sub`); keep `overflow-checks` on in release

## Avoid

```rust
// ❌ BAD for large hot state
pub vault: Account<'info, VaultState>,

// ✅ GOOD
pub vault: AccountLoader<'info, VaultState>,
```

Counter scaffold (`Account` + `InitSpace`) is temporary Day-1 sample — replace with zero-copy for production state.
